Detect arg-count mismatches in algebra/populate

Add a `arg_num_errors` map to `RuleStructures`, keyed by AST node id of
the offending site (`PredAtomId` for pred atoms, `AppTermId` for func
applications), and populate it from `walk_pred_atom` and `emit_app`
whenever a resolved pred or func disagrees on argument count. Resolution
of member preds/funcs depends on type info that propagates over the
populate/close fixed point, so re-walks can flip a previously
unresolvable site into a checked one — keying by node id keeps the
diagnostic idempotent across iterations. `build_structures` surfaces
these alongside type conflicts.

Stop iterating `pred_arg_num_should_match` /
`func_arg_num_should_match` from `semantics::check_eqlog`; the
eqlog-side rules and predicates remain defined in eqlog.eql but no
longer feed compile errors. Drop the `nat`/`nats` helpers in
`eqlog_util`, which were only consumed by the removed iterators.
